  "caption": "Quinn's workout: tiny weights, 200 reps, lots of yawning. Then came achy joints, patchy sleep and hot flushes.\n\nAround menopause, bone and muscle can decline faster, and widespread aches are common without always meaning damage. Strength training can help on both fronts.\n\nWhat often helps: two to three sessions a week with loads that feel genuinely hard by the last rep, covering squat, hinge, push, pull and carry. Add a little hopping or skipping if it suits you, practise balance, and progress your weights over time. Keep cardio, just not instead of lifting.\n\nIf you have osteoporosis, a heart condition or other health concerns, get individual advice before you start.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
